// Package apitypes is the typed HTTP API surface of better-iam, shared by the Go server and the Go client: one Go type
// per components/schemas entry of spec/api/openapi.json, the request and answer types of every route of
// spec/api/routes.json, and an operation table describing the routes.
//
// The *_gen.go files are generated by scripts/spec/gen-go-types.mjs and must not be edited; regenerate them with
//
//	node scripts/spec/gen-go-types.mjs
//
// and check them with node scripts/spec/check-generated.mjs. runtime.go and operations.go hold the hand-written helpers
// the generated code uses.
//
// # Types
//
//   - components/schemas/X is the type X. Records that go/core already defines (Tenant, Identity, Session, AuditEvent,
//     PolicyDocument, Decision, ResourceFilter, ...) are aliases of the core types, so they are never duplicated; see
//     CoreSchemas.
//   - POST {basePath}/{group}/{method} has the request body type <Group><Method>Input and the answer type
//     <Group><Method>Output (the `data` member of `{ "data": ... }`). An answer that is another schema is an alias of
//     it. The special routes authorize, authorizeMany and listAccessible have AuthorizeInput/AuthorizeOutput,
//     AuthorizeManyInput/AuthorizeManyOutput and ListAccessibleInput/ListAccessibleOutput.
//   - Op<Group><Method> is an Op[Input, Output] for that route, and Operations lists every route with its flags
//     (public, tenant-bound, cookies) as routes.json declares them.
//
// Every recorded API call of the TypeScript test suite (spec/conformance/traces) decodes into these types and encodes
// back to the same JSON (TestTraceRoundTrip). Where openapi.json disagrees with what the TypeScript server sends, the
// generator's CORRECTIONS table adjusts the generated type and says why.
//
// # Members
//
// Struct fields keep the schema's member names as JSON tags and its order. Absent and null are different JSON:
//
//   - a required member is a plain field;
//   - an optional member is a pointer (or a nil-able slice or map) tagged omitzero: nil is absent, so an empty
//     string, zero, false or an empty list is still written;
//   - a required member that may be null is a pointer without omitzero: nil is written as null;
//   - an optional member that may be null is Optional[*T] (Optional[[]T], ...): unset is absent, set with a nil value
//     is null;
//   - an optional member of unknown type is Optional[any], so that a null value is kept.
//
// Numbers are float64, as in JavaScript. String enums are string types with one constant per value; open enums
// (TypeScript's `'a' | 'b' | (string & {})`) list the known values and accept any string. Free-form objects are
// *core.Object, which keeps JavaScript property order; values of unknown type are `any`. Objects that allow members
// besides the listed ones (TypeScript index signatures) keep the others in an Extra map.
//
// # Unions
//
// An anyOf union is a struct with one pointer field per variant; exactly one is set. Encoding writes that variant.
// Decoding sets the first variant whose shape the value matches: its JSON kind, the constants it fixes (such as a
// "kind" discriminator), the members it requires and, for a closed object, the members it allows. When no variant
// matches with closed objects checked, the first match ignoring unknown members is used.
package apitypes
